<!-- Demand sized to the "Default Signal Timing" column (totals over begin=0/end=9000):
     cars=3124, trucks=1876, buses=1487, mixed=3478. Each class's total is split
     across the 14 routes below using SUMO's fixed "number" attribute (not
     probability), so the generated vehicle count matches the target exactly;
     the table's +/- values are seed-to-seed spread and aren't encoded here.
     end=9000 (2.5h) instead of the original 900s: at 900s, the single-lane
     bottleneck edges (E#11, E#15) would need ~5,700-11,400 veh/h to clear this
     demand, several times realistic signalized single-lane capacity. Spreading
     the same totals over 9000s brings the worst edge (E#15) down to ~1,140
     veh/h, within plausible single-lane capacity. -->

